    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="StoichiometricNetwork&#x27;s general mass-action engine, applied to a three-step radical chain mechanism (initiation, branching propagation, and linear termination), reproduces the qualitative signature of a chain-branching explosion: below a critical branching rate the radical concentration stays small and the fuel decays gently, while above it the radical population grows explosively and burns through the fuel in a short, sharp spike -- exactly the ignition-vs-no-ignition switch behind Semenov&#x27;s and Hinshelwood&#x27;s explosion-limit theory.">

