.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="free_radical_network builds the lumped initiation/propagation/termination kinetics as a StoichiometricNetwork and integrates it numerically. Because termination is much faster than initiator decomposition, the radical concentration relaxes almost immediately to the steady-state approximation&#x27;s closed-form prediction (~chemistrykit.polymer.systems.chain_growth.steady_state_radical_concentration) -- verified here by comparing the two directly -- while monomer is consumed only slowly, at the classic square-root-of-initiator rate.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/polymer/chain_growth/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_free_radical_kinetics_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/polymer/chain_growth/plot_01_free_radical_kinetics`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Flory's steady-state kinetics of free-radical polymerization</div>
    </div>


.. only:: not html

 * :doc:`/api/gallery/polymer/chain_growth/plot_01_free_radical_kinetics`

.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="free_radical_network&#x27;s mode argument selects between the two ways two growing radical chains can terminate: combination (they fuse into a single dead chain) or disproportionation (one radical abstracts a hydrogen from the other, producing two separate dead chains). Bevington, Melville, and Taylor (&quot;The Termination Reaction in Radical Polymerizations,&quot; J. Polym. Sci. 12 (1954), 449-459) showed how to distinguish the two experimentally, by end-group analysis and by the resulting degree of polymerization&#x27;s relationship to the kinetic chain length (~chemistrykit.polymer.systems.chain_growth.kinetic_chain_length) nu: \bar X_n = 2\nu for combination (two radicals&#x27; worth of monomer per dead chain) but \bar X_n = \nu for disproportionation (one radical&#x27;s worth per dead chain) -- verified here directly against the numerically integrated network.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/polymer/chain_growth/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_02_combination_vs_disproportionation_thumb.png
    :alt:

  :doc:`/api/gallery/polymer/chain_growth/plot_02_combination_vs_disproportionation`

.. raw:: html

      <div class="sphx-glr-thumbnail-title">Combination vs. disproportionation termination</div>
    </div>


